
# 📘 ENGLISH PROJECT

**Topic:** Poor Communication Skills Among Learners

**Grade:** ____________________
**School:** ____________________

---

## <span style="color:green;">Stage 1: Problem Identification</span>

**Problem Identification:**
Many learners have poor communication skills. They struggle to express themselves clearly when speaking or writing in English. Some learners are shy, lack confidence, or do not practise English regularly. This affects their participation in class and academic performance.

**Statement of Intent:**
To improve communication skills among learners through awareness and regular use of English.

**Project Specification:**
• Identify causes of poor communication skills
• Encourage learners to speak English confidently
• Improve writing and speaking skills
• Promote participation in class activities
• Use simple and clear messages

---

## <span style="color:green;">Stage 2: Investigation of Related Ideas</span>

**1. Classroom Discussions**

**Advantages:**
• Encourages participation
• Improves confidence
• Builds speaking skills

**Disadvantages:**
• Some learners remain shy
• Needs supervision
• Time consuming

**2. Debate and Speech Activities**

**Advantages:**
• Improves pronunciation
• Builds confidence
• Develops thinking skills

**Disadvantages:**
• Some learners fear public speaking
• Requires preparation
• Can be difficult for beginners

**3. Communication Awareness Poster (Chosen Solution)**

**Advantages:**
• Visible daily
• Easy to understand
• Encourages learners

**Disadvantages:**
• May be ignored
• Needs creativity
• Can fade over time

---

## <span style="color:green;">Stage 3: Generation of Possible Solutions</span>

**1. Reading English Books**

**Advantages:**
• Improves vocabulary
• Enhances grammar
• Builds confidence

**Disadvantages:**
• Some learners dislike reading
• Needs books
• Can take time

**2. English Speaking Clubs**

**Advantages:**
• Encourages teamwork
• Improves speaking
• Fun and interactive

**Disadvantages:**
• Not all learners participate
• Needs supervision
• Time needed

**3. Awareness Poster (Chosen Solution)**

**Advantages:**
• Simple and clear
• Low cost
• Seen by many learners

**Disadvantages:**
• Limited explanation
• May be ignored
• Needs proper placement

---

## <span style="color:green;">Stage 4: Refinement of the Chosen Idea</span>

**Chosen Solution:** Communication Awareness Poster

**Reasons:**
• Easy to make
• Low cost
• Encourages confidence
• Promotes communication daily

**Materials Used:**
• Chart paper
• Markers
• Colour pens
• Pencil and ruler
• Pictures of learners communicating
• Glue

**Where It Will Be Placed:**
• Classroom
• Library
• Corridor
• Notice board

---

## <span style="color:green;">Stage 5: Presentation of Final Solution (POSTER PROMPT)</span>

**TITLE:**
🗣️ SPEAK ENGLISH WITH CONFIDENCE!

**MAIN DRAWING:**
• Learners discussing happily
• Speech bubbles with English words
• Books and pencils

**MESSAGES:**
• Communication builds confidence
• Speak English every day
• Good communication improves learning

**PROBLEMS SECTION:**
• Fear of speaking
• Lack of confidence
• Limited English practice

**SOLUTIONS SECTION:**
• Practise speaking daily
• Read English books
• Join speaking clubs
• Participate in class discussions

**SLOGAN:**
👉 “Good communication leads to success!”

---

## <span style="color:green;">Stage 6: Evaluation and Recommendations</span>

**Relevance to Statement of Intent:**
The poster encouraged learners to improve their communication skills and participate more confidently in class activities.

**Challenges Faced:**
• Some learners ignored the poster
• Limited materials
• Needs creativity

**Recommendations:**
• Use bright colours
• Place posters in busy areas
• Encourage daily English speaking
• Update posters regularly
